# Living notes

When the owner states a **new or changed** product intent, update the matching file in the same turn (do not wait to be asked):

| They talk about | File |
| --- | --- |
| Structure, routing, FSM vs workspace, Hermes/Gemini, HITL gates, data paths, GPU/mount rules | [`work/ARCHITECTURE_POINTS.md`](work/ARCHITECTURE_POINTS.md) |
| Look, layout, motion, React Bits, workspace skins, copy, interaction | [`work/UI_UX_POINTS.md`](work/UI_UX_POINTS.md) |
| A capability they want Jarvis to do (or stop doing) | [`work/APP_FEATURES.md`](work/APP_FEATURES.md) |

How:

1. Add a dated **Log** bullet with their words distilled.
2. If it is a decision (not just an idea), fold it into **Current lock** and drop the contradiction.
3. Touch only the file(s) that changed. Do not rewrite `VISION_WORKBOOK.md` unless they ask.

These notes are the conversation record. `docs/CURRENT.md` is as-built. Do not invent features into the notes.
